# Operational Safety Rules

## Kill Switch & Dry Run
- Add and honor `HALT` (bool/int) at the **last mile** before any sign/send. If `HALT=1`, log `HALT_ACTIVE` and return early.
- Add and honor `DRY_RUN` (bool). If `DRY_RUN=true`, never sign or send a transaction. Instead:
  - Log `WOULD_BUY` / `WOULD_SELL` with full context (mint, size, slippage, priority fee).
  - Call the portfolio simulator (see portfolio-sim.mdc).
- Default to **DRY_RUN=true** in examples and docs.

## Secrets
- Never print `SOLANA_PRIVATE_KEY` or any secrets to logs or diffs.
- Do not invent new env var names; use the canonical names only.

## Minimal Diffs
- Make minimal, localized hooks at the send-tx site(s); no refactors unless explicitly requested.
